+++ b/packages/ffmpeg-0166-avcodec-aac-take-a-missing-sample-rate-from-the-conf.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Trevor Hansen <trev_abroad@yahoo.com>
+Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:06:05 +1100
+Subject: [PATCH 166/178] avcodec/aac: take a missing sample rate from the
+ configuration in the ER frame path
+
+The error-resilient output path never sets avctx->sample_rate from the
+stream configuration; it copies whatever the caller supplied into the
+output frame. The general-audio path and USAC both set it from the
+parsed configuration. AAC declares AV_CODEC_CAP_CHANNEL_CONF, so
+avcodec_open2() accepts a context with no sample rate, and a valid ER
+stream whose rate is only in its AudioSpecificConfig then outputs a
+frame with sample rate 0, which frame_validate() rejects with
+AVERROR_BUG (and which trips the av_assert0() in the decode fuzzer).
+
+When the caller supplied no sample rate, take it from the configuration
+before outputting the frame, so that such streams decode. A sample rate
+supplied by the caller is left alone, so nothing changes for streams
+that decode today.
+
+An ER object type can only be selected by a configuration with a valid
+sampling index, so the rate should always be positive after this;
+reject a non-positive one anyway, with the same message and error code
+as the general-audio path.
+
+Signed-off-by: Trevor Hansen <trev_abroad@yahoo.com>
+(cherry picked from commit 3f18b1398a577b8d3367daf4695bdb64fcae208f)
+---
+ libavcodec/aac/aacdec.c | 9 +++++++++
+ 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)
+
+diff --git a/libavcodec/aac/aacdec.c b/libavcodec/aac/aacdec.c
+index 2f47ce0569..7dbbf4afaa 100644
+--- a/libavcodec/aac/aacdec.c
++++ b/libavcodec/aac/aacdec.c
+@@ -2224,6 +2224,15 @@ static int aac_decode_er_frame(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVFrame *frame,
+ 
+     spectral_to_sample(ac, samples);
+ 
++    if (avctx->sample_rate <= 0)
++        avctx->sample_rate = m4ac->sample_rate;
++
++    if (avctx->sample_rate <= 0) {
++        av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR,
++               "Cannot output a frame without a valid sample rate\n");
++        return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
++    }
++
+     if (!ac->frame->data[0] && samples) {
+         av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "no frame data found\n");
+         return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
diff --git a/packages/ffmpeg-0167-avcodec-aac-do-not-return-AVERROR_BUG-for-an-unsuppo.patch b/packages/ffmpeg-0167-avcodec-aac-do-not-return-AVERROR_BUG-for-an-unsuppo.patch
