+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Behdad Esfahbod <behdad@behdad.org>
+Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:33:50 -0600
+Subject: [PATCH 1/5] [truetype] Use the blend axis count for private VARC
+ axes.
+
+Static VARC fonts can have private variation axes without an 'fvar'
+table or public MM metadata.  Use the blend's axis count when validating
+'avar' and item variation stores, avoiding a null 'mmvar' dereference
+when loading HVAR or VVAR for a VARC component.
+
+* src/truetype/ttgxvar.c (ft_var_load_avar,
+  tt_var_load_item_variation_store): Use blend->num_axis.
+
+* tests/varc/make-hvvar-fonts.py: Generate HVAR and VVAR fixtures from
+  the static VARC/gvar font using only Python's standard library.
+* tests/meson.build: Generate the fixtures and pass them to the VARC test.
+* tests/varc/main.c (test_font, main): Test generated fixture paths.
+
+Tests: all five Meson regression tests pass.
+
+Fixes issue #1474.
+
+Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex
